const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文联系股票价格、盈余与预期股利，讨论这些会计和现金流信息在估值中的位置。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"“Stock Prices, Earnings, and Expected Dividends” frames a bounded research question. Read the stated question together with the named sample, dates, and institutional setting rather than treating it as a conclusion that automatically travels to another market or period."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.1988.tb04598.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (1988) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (1988) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"公开研究描述比较价格与盈余、股利预期之间的关系，依赖会计期间、披露时点和预测变量的处理。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"For “Stock Prices, Earnings, and Expected Dividends”, the source describes a deliberate comparison, observation window, and control relation. Those choices are part of its research contract: changing one can change the proposition being tested, even when the method label remains the same."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.1988.tb04598.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (1988) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (1988) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"必须区分财年末、公告日、可用日、经修订盈余与股利口径；这些不是一个同义的“基本面日期”。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"For “Stock Prices, Earnings, and Expected Dividends”, keep the fields, their availability timing, and the sample filters separate from the original study. A same-named variable, later-revised database, or matching end-of-period date is not automatically a comparable input."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.1988.tb04598.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (1988) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (1988) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"来源所讨论的是估值信息之间的关系，不表示报告盈余能机械决定下一期价格变化。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"For “Stock Prices, Earnings, and Expected Dividends”, the source supports only the empirical or theoretical relation it describes. It does not turn association, model fit, or historical performance into causality, a directly executable procedure, or a guarantee about subsequent outcomes."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.1988.tb04598.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (1988) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (1988) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"保留原始报表版本和发布日期，统一单位与拆分调整，并避免使用之后修订的字段进行历史排序。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Before extending “Stock Prices, Earnings, and Expected Dividends”, record its sample, timing, construction choices, and source edition in a versioned note. Keep the primary-source link and access date so a later reader can distinguish a changed definition from a changed result."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.1988.tb04598.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (1988) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (1988) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 The Journal of Finance (1988)。会计数据跨制度和公司并不完全可比，价格反应还受预期、风险和市场摩擦影响。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites The Journal of Finance (1988) for “Stock Prices, Earnings, and Expected Dividends”. Its public description defines the boundary. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-6261.1988.tb04598.x",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (1988) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (1988) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Stock Prices, Earnings, and Expected Dividends”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。会计数据跨制度和公司并不完全可比，价格反应还受预期、风险和市场摩擦影响。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Stock Prices, Earnings, and Expected Dividends”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
